    "field": "Aerosol absorption",
    "problem": "Estimating the climate impact of absorbing aerosols is hindered by significant uncertainties in both observations and models regarding aerosol composition, optical properties, mixing state, and vertical distribution, which makes constraining total aerosol absorption challenging.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a roadmap to better constrain aerosol absorption by combining modeling with in-situ and satellite observations, improving observational capabilities, and fostering better dialogue and consistent terminology within the scientific community to reduce uncertainties in climate models.",
    "task": "The task is to review recent progress toward constraining global and regional aerosol absorption of solar radiation by synthesizing findings from observations and modeling to better understand the influences of aerosols on the climate.",
